[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "260726-kekkai-packet-device"
  :adr/title "A host-owned packet-device capability isolates privileged OS tunnel I/O"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-26"
  :adr/body "# Packet device capability\n\n## Decision\n\n`aiueos:capability@0.4.0` introduces one host-owned `packet-device` resource for Kekkai Network Extension, VpnService, and desktop TUN adapters. A `.kotoba` guest cannot open an OS descriptor, construct or serialize a device handle, select an unadmitted route, or access ambient sockets. The host creates the resource only after admission and binds MTU, full-route flags, packet size, inflight quota, expiry, revocation epoch, and audit identity to the grant.\n\n## Enforcement\n\nEvery read and write validates IP family, declared length, MTU, the signed Kekkai route edge, byte/item quota, revocation, and audit availability. Failure is denial. Relay and public management endpoints are excluded by the privileged host before a full default route is installed, preventing recursive capture. Raw IP is never sent to a relay without the independently authenticated Kekkai transport.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nVersion 0.3.0 remains unchanged. Compiler lowering for 0.4.0 is not implied by the WIT contract; until typed lowering is admitted, `kekkai.packet-plane` is compiled as a pure native/Wasm decision module and privileged adapters invoke its scalar decision entry through the verified Kotoba host ABI."}]
